# Example engine config for bin/ops / the nightly timer.
# Copy to /home/ali/.config/skynet-ops/ops.env on vm-skynet-ops (0600). No secrets belong here.
# The nightly unit reads it via EnvironmentFile=-; edits take effect on the next run (no reload).
#
# systemd's EnvironmentFile does NOT strip inline '# comments' — everything after '=' is the
# literal value. Keep comments on their OWN line; never trail one after an assignment.

# Primary + fallback engine for the optional nightly narrative/audit stage; scripts/nightly.sh owns preparation/finalization.
# OPS_ENGINE: codex | claude
OPS_ENGINE=codex
# OPS_ENGINE_FALLBACK: codex | claude | none  (default: the OTHER engine)
# OPS_ENGINE_FALLBACK=claude

# Model per engine (unset = engine default)
# OPS_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-5-codex
# OPS_CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8

# Other knobs
# OPS_NIGHTLY_MODE=script  → force the deterministic path, skip LLMs entirely
# OPS_NIGHTLY_MODE=script
# OPS_ENGINE_CMD  → full override of the PRIMARY command, e.g.:
# OPS_ENGINE_CMD='codex exec --full-auto --model X'
# Nightly auto-merge is hard-suspended (AGENTS.md §3). This legacy setting has no
# effect until a later human-reviewed restoration of the capability.
# OPS_NIGHTLY_AUTOMERGE=0
